    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0267" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/5–1054: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the United States Delegation</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret<lb/>niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-10T11:48:00-04:00">May 10, 1954—11:48
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Tosec 114. Department’s Tosec 111 sent Seoul 904 and Tokyo 2468;<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d139-f1"/> Seoul’s 1139<anchor n="2" xml:id="d139-f2"/> and
                        1140<anchor n="3" xml:id="d139-f3"/> repeated Geneva 64 and 65 Tokyo 673 and
                    675. Department has reconsidered and does not desire discussion Plan B with
                    working group in Geneva mentioned in paragraph 1 reference Department
                    telegram.</p>
                <pb facs="0268" n="242" xml:id="pg242"/>
                <p>Increasing seriousness Indochina situation underlines undesirability open break
                    with Rhee over presentation Plan B which
                    we like him recognize has serious practical difficulties if Communists were to
                    accept. Efforts persuade him agree to presentation Plan B should continue along
                    lines already indicated. Especially desirable have Pyun recommend it from Geneva if not already done.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
